<!--{ lb01 : rich }-->
# 14. Your own libraries

*Advanced.* A library is a document that gives names to values and
functions for other documents to use: material properties, load factors,
the checks of a design code. You write it once, and every document of the
project imports it. About six minutes.
<!--{ lb02 : rich }-->
## Write a library

1. In the navigation pane, right-click the folder `lib` and choose
   **New folder…**. Name it `beams`.
2. Right-click `beams` and choose **New document…**. Name it `index`.
3. In the new document, write a title line, *Beam formulas*. Then press
   **Alt+Enter** for a line below, press **=**, and write the function of
   lesson 13: `moment = (q, L) -> q * L ^ 2 / 8`.
4. Save with **Ctrl+S**, and come back here with the browser's back button.
<!--{ lb03 : markdown }-->
## Use it

**Your turn.** On the empty line just above the check below, press **=** and
write the import of your library:

`texl.import "~/lib/beams/index.texl" ~> (lib -> bind "beams" lib.data)`
<!--{ lb04 : rich }-->

<!--{ lb05 : formula }-->
<% tutorial.check (beams.moment (10, 4) == 20) %>
<!--{ lb06 : markdown }-->
With your library, a load of 12.5 kN/m on a span of 6 m gives a moment of
**<% beams.moment (12.5, 6) ; "…" %> kNm**.
<!--{ lb07 : rich }-->
## How libraries work

- An imported document is computed on its own: it does not see the names of
  the document that imports it. So it gives the same values to everybody.
- `bind "beams" lib.data` gives all the names of the library one name in
  your document, so they never clash with yours: `beams.moment`.
- The library is read again every time your document is computed. Change
  it, save, and every document that imports it follows.
- In a project, keep libraries in `lib`, one folder each, and import them
  with `~`. To give a library to a colleague, give them its folder: they
  copy it into their project's `lib`.
- An address can also be a full web address, `https://…`, of a document on
  another server that allows it.

More in the manual: [Documents and imports](https://www.onlabs.org/manual/templates/documents.html)
and [Projects and libraries](https://www.onlabs.org/manual/editor/projects.html).
<!--{ lb08 : rich }-->
